# Captain Truck — Locked Stack & Repo Scope

## This repository builds
- NestJS custom backend (TypeScript) — `backend/`
- React admin dashboard (Vite + Tailwind), hosted on Vercel — `admin/`
- Flutter **Customer** app (Android) — `mobile_apps/customer_app/`
- Vendored UI deps (e.g. liquid glass) — `mobile_apps/vendor/`

## Do NOT build in this repo yet
- Flutter **Driver** app (separate folder/repo later)

## Locked technologies (do not substitute)
| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Backend | NestJS + TypeScript |
| Realtime | Socket.IO |
| Database | PostgreSQL (Neon free) |
| Cache | Redis (Upstash free or on Oracle VM) |
| Auth | Custom JWT + refresh tokens (roles: customer, driver, admin) |
| Push | FCM only (not full Firebase) |
| Files | Cloudinary |
| Maps/routing | OSM: Nominatim, Photon, OSRM (mobile: flutter_map) |
| On-device AI | TFLite cost prediction + ML Kit Smart Reply (mobile) |
| Customer UI | Flutter + **BLoC** + `liquid_glass_renderer` (vendored from GitHub) |
| Payments | Cash-on-Pickup **and** Stripe **Test Mode** |
| API host | Oracle Cloud Always Free VM |
| Admin host | Vercel |
| Language | TypeScript (API/admin); Dart (customer Flutter) |

## Product surfaces
1. Customer Flutter app — Android only — `mobile_apps/customer_app/`
2. Driver Flutter app — Android only — later / separate
3. Admin web panel — this repo
4. Shared NestJS API — this repo

## In-scope features (do not remove)
- Admin-mediated driver/truck assignment
- 2–3 OSM route options + AI trip cost
- Realtime GPS tracking (Socket.IO)
- Chat: text, image, voice + Smart Reply (mobile) + 90-day auto-delete
- Cash-on-Pickup + commission ledger
- Stripe Test Mode payments
- Role-based auth (customer / driver / admin)

## Constraints
- Prefer free tiers only (FYP budget = $0)
- Optimize for low latency (no cold-start PaaS for the API)
- Keep APIs mobile-ready (REST + Socket.IO)
- Customer app phases gated like backend/admin (`CUSTOMER_PHASE_PLAN.md`)

## When unsure
Ask before adding paid services, Firebase (beyond FCM), MongoDB, GraphQL, or a third client beyond customer Flutter + admin.
